 "name": "Causality",
 "description": "Proofs that need assumptions and sums (PQP ch. 8). A proof can assume things about its symbols — Φ causal, U unitary — shown in the bar above the steps; every check then uses random values satisfying them. Composing causal processes is causal; measuring is causal (a sum over a basis, Σᵢ); a unitary undoes itself; a doubled isometry is causal; and Σᵢ |i⟩⟨i| is the identity.",
